---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Community Guidelines"
  description="How to keep the K-Decoded Community kind, useful, and welcoming."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <a href="/community" class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-700 hover:underline">← Back to Community</a>

    <div class="mt-5 rounded-3xl border border-brand-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-brand-700">K-Decoded Community</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Community guidelines</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-gray-600">A warm, useful place for sharing K-beauty finds, Korea travel tips, language questions, and thoughtful perspectives.</p>

      <div class="prose prose-brand mt-9 max-w-none">
        <h2>Keep it kind</h2>
        <p>Address ideas, not people. Harassment, hate speech, threats, sexual content, and personal attacks are not welcome.</p>

        <h2>Make it useful</h2>
        <p>Stay reasonably on topic, add context to questions, and share personal experience honestly. It is fine to disagree—do so respectfully.</p>

        <h2>No spam or scams</h2>
        <p>Do not post misleading links, affiliate-link spam, unsolicited promotions, impersonation, phishing attempts, or requests for private information.</p>

        <h2>Respect privacy and ownership</h2>
        <p>Do not share someone else’s private details. Post only material you have the right to share, and credit creators when appropriate.</p>

        <h2>How moderation works</h2>
        <p>You can report a topic or reply using its Report button. Moderators may hide, edit, lock, or remove content that breaks these guidelines, and may suspend accounts that repeatedly do so.</p>

        <h2>Need help?</h2>
        <p>If you see harmful content, report it rather than engaging with it. We aim to keep the Community calm, welcoming, and useful for everyone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
